# Mobile Patterns

## Lot Data — Always Use the Static Wrapper

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — data comes from bundled JSON, zero network calls
import { getAllLots, getLotById, applyOccupancy, type RutgersLot } from '@/data/lots';
import { ENABLE_ALL_CAMPUSES } from '@/constants/featureFlags';

const lots = getAllLots(ENABLE_ALL_CAMPUSES);
const lot = getLotById('10001'); // lot_id is always a string like "10001"

// ❌ WRONG — never fetch lot metadata from the backend
const res = await authApiCall('/lots');
const res = await authApiCall(`/lots/${id}`);
```

## Live Occupancy — Supabase Realtime

Occupancy counts come from `lot_occupancy` via `useQuery` + Realtime subscription (see `app/(tabs)/index.tsx`).
Use `applyOccupancy(lots, occupancyMap)` to merge live counts into static lot data.

## API Calls

```typescript
import { authApiCall } from '@/lib/supabase';    // authenticated (park, friends, favorites)
import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase-client'; // direct Supabase client for Realtime
```

`publicApiCall` is only for unauthenticated endpoints. Prefer `authApiCall` for everything user-scoped.

## Offline

- Map always loads (data is bundled). 
- Session start/end actions queue via `OfflineQueue` when offline and replay on reconnect.
- Do not cache lot data locally — it's already in the bundle.

## Feature Flags

```typescript
import { ENABLE_ALL_CAMPUSES, OFFLINE_QUEUE_ENABLED } from '@/constants/featureFlags';
```

`ENABLE_ALL_CAMPUSES` gates non-New Brunswick lots. Off by default.
